You could smell your enemy's scent everywhere. Your acute beastly hearing detected some noise coming from the room on the second floor. You silently ran up the stairs and took a peek through a slightly opened door. It was him! The culprit of your misery.  You instantly felt a burst of rage. You wanted to kill him when suddenly wind brought the forest smell through the window. You remembered the feeling of freedom and strength while you had been a wolf. The understanding that you don't want to part with the wolf came to your mind. But you wanted to revenge anyway. After you had taken enough pleasure in seeing your enemy trembling with fear, you knocked him to the floor. You bit his arm and ran into the forest. Let him feel some of the suffering you'd felt because of him! That was fair.